answer-field/id #uuid "1a7341a7-fa0a-54fe-b478-20dd9864726e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479284}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e51262c4-111b-5af6-9c4b-384b623d1a51" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int sec⁡x(3sec⁡x+8tan⁡x)\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int sec⁡xtan⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =sec⁡x+C, \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =tan⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int sec⁡x(3sec⁡x+8tan⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{sec}^{2}⁡x+8sec⁡xtan⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 3{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 8sec⁡xtan⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+8\\int sec⁡xtan⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3tan⁡x+8sec⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Secant Squared"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096843 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096402 :question/id #uuid "2c37ae73-233d-5e0d-87ff-05cacc6d078b" :question/math-academy-id "e-183" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-3x}},$ calculate $f'(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=1-3x$ and $f(g(x)) = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{g}} = g^{-1/2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{-1/2}{)}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{2}{g}^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{2{g}^{3/2}}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(1-3x{)}^{′}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{g}^{3/2}}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2{g}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2(1-3x{)}^{3/2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0a312840-0d35-50bb-94b3-b04778f4efc3" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096972 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd726c27-0178-5cc8-a8b6-82e60d62ac1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.typ