/problem "Given that $f(x)={(3x+4)}^{5},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=3x+4$ and $f(g(x))=g(x{)}^{5}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{5}{)}^{′}=5{g}^{4}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(3x+4{)}^{′}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =5{g}^{4}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =15(3x+4{)}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317327 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc8b5aee-000a-5a8d-818f-e20c5debd3ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20(4x+3)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc8b5aee-000a-5a8d-818f-e20c5debd3ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20(4x+3)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316184} :answer-field/id #uuid "625a79d7-54d7-570b-aa7c-729d582ac660" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316778}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ebc59fe-5ccc-59b1-9757-9c760459c2ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-342804" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={(4x+3)}^{5},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=4x+3$ and $f(g(x))=g(x{)}^{5}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{5}{)}^{′}=5{g}^{4}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(4x+3{)}^{′}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =5{g}^{4}\\cdot (4) \\\\  & =20(4x+3{)}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317333 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8817f05b-018c-5853-b6cc-e00880617a94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8817f05b-018c-5853-b6cc-e00880617a94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315880} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5ab2d60-fecd-56b2-a6fc-370a03381af0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317093}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2fb4db78-694f-5845-af11-624db7bcff81" :question/math-academy-id "q-342875" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={({x}^{5}-4{x}^{4})}^{2},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=2({x}^{5}-4{x}^{4})($\n{{field-1}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)={x}^{5}-4{x}^{4}$ and $f(g(x))=g(x)^{2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{2})^{′}=2g, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{5}-4{x}^{4})^{′}=5{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =2g\\cdot (5{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =2({x}^{5}-4{x}^{4})(\\,5{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317335 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54037730-2600-58cb-b40d-648fd184a076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54037730-2600-58cb-b40d-648fd184a076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315600} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f9abe6a-bb3b-59b2-9f07-73fdde4dcc36" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316583}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6a140a75-4d09-557b-baa7-d7202838dd2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-342883" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\sqrt{5x-4},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=5x-4$ and $f(g(x))=\\sqrt{g(x)}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & ={(\\sqrt{g})}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(5x-4)^{′}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317336 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d665e027-6ab2-5ec3-82b7-84f4dddc219b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-4{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d665e027-6ab2-5ec3-82b7-84f4dddc219b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-4{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316315} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1297ade-d13c-5373-bff2-2ee35469ee63" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317084}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "49fe03e2-8c48-5c16-b76a-8505b327ec2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-342891" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}+5}},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}+5{)}^{3}}}($\n{{field-1}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=2{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}+5$ and $f(g(x))=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{g(x)}}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & ={(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{g}})}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{g}^{3}}}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(2{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}+5{)}^{′}=8{x}^{3}-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{g}^{3}}}\\cdot (8{x}^{3}-2x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}+5{)}^{3}}}(\\,x-4{x}^{3}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c5aa34c-80