dent :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20(4x+6)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493335} :answer-field/id #uuid "74945d2f-3779-5856-8f0b-b1fe26940f82" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493329}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c698fb8-2f47-52aa-ab20-d02b17699d11" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={(4x+6)}^{5},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=4x+6$ and $f(g(x))=g(x{)}^{5}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{5}{)}^{′}=5{g}^{4}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(4x+6{)}^{′}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =5{g}^{4}\\cdot (4) \\\\  & =20(4x+6{)}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e6b327a-95b5-56cb-b8b1-80852501eb0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e6b327a-95b5-56cb-b8b1-80852501eb0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493327} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a534b2c-8471-58d8-901e-8ca326167938" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493328}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "97e8ab80-425a-5ce3-aeca-1b6c32080f6d" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\sqrt{5x-3},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=5x-3$ and $f(g(x))=\\sqrt{g(x)}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & ={(\\sqrt{g})}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(5x-3)^{′}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493332 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df5e2ea6-5eec-545e-bf02-640b9eb005aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{4}-28{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df5e2ea6-5eec-545e-bf02-640b9eb005aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{4}-28{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493334} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9beb5af-bf72-501b-8c38-28d625a4d182" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493333}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a645231c-c79c-561b-9b41-b96c53332e19" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={({x}^{5}-7{x}^{4})}^{2},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=2({x}^{5}-7{x}^{4})($\n{{field-1}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)={x}^{5}-7{x}^{4}$ and $f(g(x))=g(x)^{2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{2})^{′}=2g, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{5}-7{x}^{4})^{′}=5{x}^{4}-28{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =2g\\cdot (5{x}^{4}-28{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =2({x}^{5}-7{x}^{4})(\\,5{x}^{4}-28{x}^{3}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Function Using the Chain Rule and Prime Notation"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100725 :question/id #uuid "e092e191-84ac-5d9f-b0db-94d628a6154e" :question/math-academy-id "e-525" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny' = -\\dfrac{y}{x}, \\qquad x \\neq 0\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{x}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f'(x) = -\\dfrac{1}{x^2}$\n\n- Substituting $y = f(x)$ and $y' = f'(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n\n- The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Differentiating $f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{x},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(\\frac{1}{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y = \\dfrac{1}{x}$ and $y' = -\\dfrac{1}{x^2}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}-\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & \\overset{?}{=}-\\frac{(\\frac{1}{x})}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y = \\dfrac{1}{x}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048593 :topic/math-academy-id 35 :topic/title "The Power Rule for Differentiation"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049592 :topic/math-academy-id 3215 :topic/title "Introduction to Differential Equations"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050271 :topic/math-academy-id 1007 :topic/title "The Chain Rule With Exponential Functions"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050690 :topic/math-academy-id 1116 :topic/title "Differentiating Logarithmic Functions"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050789 :topic/math-academy-id 305 :topic/title "The Chain Rule With Trigonometric Functions"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101155 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8245f03-8a88-51b1-816d-b194c8191459" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437920} {:answer/id #uuid "241c8aac-057f-5bd8-8672-538887a90f96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8245f03-8a88-51b1-816d-b194c8191459" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437920} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8022058-91f7-5a21-86f8-cda411ec1bea" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438989} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95795348-591c-5f80-a9dc-9d6695fa2629" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437922} {:answer/id #uuid "e733e51a-85ca-5ec8-b45a-8579524491ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e733e51a-85ca-5ec8-b45a-8579524491ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437923} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8576006-7ef6-5181-a3ea-35a1c7c390e2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438990} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f72c83c-eb8c-5631-b3a6-b174e90aab92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437924} {:answer/id #uuid "589c074c-f210-5e65-911b-aa087fdb7ec5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "589c074c-f210-5e65-911b-aa087fdb7ec5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437925} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e1d7437-eee9-54ee-a6bc-2720730fc72d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438991}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b2e480d-7f17-59ba-a02c-a786007bf39b" :question/math-academy-id "q-140631" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{4y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)={x}^{4}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=5{x}^{5}.$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)={x}^{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{4})^{′} \\\\  & =4{x}^{3} \\\\  & \\ne 5{x}^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y={x}^{4}$ and ${y}^{′}=4{x}^{3}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4y}{x} \\\\ (4{x}^{3}) & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4({x}^{4})}{x} \\\\ 4{x}^{3} & =4{x}^{3}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y={x}^{4}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101157 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df433686-7b08-5422-9159-68e30b1dd3b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437926} {:answer/id #uuid "be8d3f83-dbd7-5512-8e52-cbb77918ee9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be8d3f83-dbd7-5512-8e52-cbb77918ee9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437927} :answer-field/id #uuid "3da2476a-cd94-5d52-b20c-ba45588a2e94" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438992} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "697f7e93-3daf-5d09-aaa0-33a0a696b34b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437928} {:answer/id #uuid "66aac766-51f7-5829-b96d-8fdbe93a04eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66aac766-51f7-5829-b96d-8fdbe93a04eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437929} :answer-field/id #uuid "13228480-d8e3-59b9-a952-c0a713529199" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438993} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bbf35f7-eca9-5cd8-a4bb-3916780464ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437930} {:answer/id #uuid "e90e9605-ee1b-56aa-a246-8f89f26d5c61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e90e9605-ee1b-56aa-a246-8f89f26d5c61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437931} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a4b74fc-fbff-523b-9711-9570469a2063" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438994}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47b66471-b70f-5509-8368-6a6674b74447" :question/math-academy-id "q-141078" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2y\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)={e}^{2x}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=2{e}^{2x}$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Differentiating $f(x)={e}^{2x},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({e}^{2x})}^{′} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y={e}^{2x}$ and ${y}^{′}=2{e}^{2x}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}2y \\\\ 2{e}^{2x} & =2{e}^{2x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y={e}^{2x}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272196 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58cf84e4-bf37-53ee-9c4e-c48312865eba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437932} {:answer/id #uuid "7c777b71-5609-57b6-98cd-5de6ad97f13e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58cf84e4-bf37-53ee-9c4e-c48312865eba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437932} :answer-field/id #uuid "1754ff84-62e2-5fa6-b4ab-1a4ed225ccf5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438995} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd869c55-39da-53e6-ae83-c00f9f75727e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437934} {:answer/id #uuid "3ebf7563-afa0-50f3-97cb-0e17f76f6a4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd869c55-39da-53e6-ae83-c00f9f75727e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437934} :answer-field/id #uuid "94674f44-214d-51de-8806-6b7b3a2c49aa" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438996} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68878cd7-dc72-5e55-800f-d9aceba0d493" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437936} {:answer/id #uuid "5695c90a-25d5-5c15-8845-780cd00f9341" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68878cd7-dc72-5e55-800f-d9aceba0d493" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437936} :answer-field/id #uuid "b41c643e-8038-5852-a780-537545979885" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438997}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5c28aa3d-73cf-552e-9e05-dfc5bcb67151" :question/math-academy-id "q-141080" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2y\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\  & \\ne 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ and ${y}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ into the original equation, we get a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}2y \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}2(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\ne \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272197 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc440dfb-329e-5cce-98e2-d61a73c6573b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437938} {:answer/id #uuid "eb3e6505-7161-5f6a-be56-c236d5b1a400" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb3e6505-7161-5f6a-be56-c236d5b1a400" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437939} :answer-field/id #uuid "062dd2dc-b6ff-50a1-9e87-20f44d397210" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438998} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97fcaffe-490b-50d3-bd81-11d7998b6387" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437940} {:answer/id #uuid "bfde07d3-eb9e-55be-b75d-2f6e35461ba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97fcaffe-490b-50d3-bd81-11d7998b6387" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437940} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e330e7c-b25a-5b7f-9f95-b68a2feb22aa" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438999} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60c19038-4ad6-599a-bc53-f97ce9ff756a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437942} {:answer/id #uuid "22a53b8b-e4ab-51f5-a137-7c3a442b5a2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60c19038-4ad6-599a-bc53-f97ce9ff756a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437942} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad20673a-9803-59bc-b2e5-d66a0d3efe10" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439000}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "82065c87-2fb6-51b8-8d32-9c57d0719fb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-141081" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Differentiating $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)}^{′} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ and ${y}^{′}=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ into the original equation, we get a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x & \\ne {cos}^{2}⁡2x\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76321bcd-1dfe-54f5-8624-a1897a3eb02d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437944} {:answer/id #uuid "74e24dca-87ac-5021-88ea-6d2cad76cfe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74e24dca-87ac-5021-88ea-6d2cad76cfe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437945} :answer-field/id #uuid "96ed6203-45be-5de5-bbe2-94c88e917af6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439001} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83ec8f2a-644e-5350-a178-f851274405b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437946} {:answer/id #uuid "f48e3736-83c7-5b2f-8b2a-b7622b40ed4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f48e3736-83c7-5b2f-8b2a-b7622b40ed4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437947} :answer-field/id #uuid "9225aa09-89ea-55c4-8ca6-de93ab83d375" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439002} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67767ab0-4e77-5125-a2ab-a6302dab16e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437948} {:answer/id #uuid "adffa49b-1f3c-5361-8969-94df35c322c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adffa49b-1f3c-5361-8969-94df35c322c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437949} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecd1164d-c8c5-54ab-8801-2a7ea56a251e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439003}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b7a88f7-a074-5f69-9224-f1585f849cc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-141082" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{e}^{y}}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Differentiating $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ and ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{1}{{e}^{y}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & =\\frac{1}{x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272199 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9eb1ace-da7e-5399-a3fe-3eca3341dc04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437950} {:answer/id #uuid "8294de83-bfe6-5d3e-907f-46fca51b308f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9eb1ace-da7e-5399-a3fe-3eca3341dc04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437950} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f826ec9-1240-515d-9e72-2dd14068a0b0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439004} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "307652cb-8dec-5139-b1b9-8b42d2c243ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437952} {:answer/id #uuid "d0fc6fa1-75d1-54ae-a895-4bd473e2976a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "307652cb-8dec-5139-b1b9-8b42d2c243ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437952} :answer-field/id #uuid "93d26810-7687-5dab-8301-97c0074dc993" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439005} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "430fce2c-320b-5e26-93df-7d20527603a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437954} {:answer/id #uuid "4dee6609-1868-55be-9c34-9e4174a83b33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "430fce2c-320b-5e26-93df-7d20527603a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437954} :answer-field/id #uuid "81855480-1021-5030-8cb7-a5a2db6e6e14" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439006}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4402732-29b4-541b-a6e6-a372fd33bf97" :question/math-academy-id "q-141084" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}},\\,x\\ne 0\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\  & \\ne -\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ and ${y}^{′}=\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}$ into the original equation, we get a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} & \\ne -\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272200 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "654fa534-773a-593f-977c-52c967bc6758" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437956} {:answer/id #uuid "3e1670b2-e9d2-5154-a206-4f8b1150ce6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "654fa534-773a-593f-977c-52c967bc6758" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437956} :answer-field/id #uuid "3757fe80-c2f2-5c86-bda7-b8b1794c555f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439007} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7283afb-092e-5737-a0c8-37560698d7cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437958} {:answer/id #uuid "23367094-d892-5aa7-a778-191ce481dae0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437959}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7283afb-092e-5737-a0c8-37560698d7cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437958} :answer-field/id #uuid "517f6faa-1205-51b0-a3ed-acee4119eb37" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439008} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80cf2045-8273-57f1-bbce-39810be44be4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437960} {:answer/id #uuid "814d7525-ee34-5bf5-a23b-7ddd661f2801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80cf2045-8273-57f1-bbce-39810be44be4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437960} :answer-field/id #uuid "da8265e0-a0fc-5f6a-becf-ca88b952fcad" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439009}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "33a5a8c7-40f0-5353-a590-88087e77753a" :question/math-academy-id "q-141086" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3y\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=3{e}^{-x}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=3{e}^{-x}$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=3{e}^{-x},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(3{e}^{-x})}^{′} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{-x} \\\\  & \\ne 3{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=3{e}^{-x}$ and ${y}^{′}=-3{e}^{-x}$ into the original equation, we get a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}-3y \\\\ -3{e}^{-x} & \\overset{?}{=}-3(3{e}^{-x}) \\\\ -3{e}^{-x} & \\ne -9{e}^{-x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=3{e}^{-x}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272201 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce779982-5956-53ce-8f93-98847edcb147" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437962} {:answer/id #uuid "20333a47-4e71-5ec5-9d41-91782cb4b909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce779982-5956-53ce-8f93-98847edcb147" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437962} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cefe8de-ad3c-5341-b5a8-44e7ce7436d0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439010} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4113f3b5-d089-56b5-ba2d-bdb03486c6dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437964} {:answer/id #uuid "1edc75ea-b6e2-5bab-aebd-7ef159ff5c58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1edc75ea-b6e2-5bab-aebd-7ef159ff5c58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437965} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1cc3bda-6bd3-5d8e-bcf2-7853efc526c4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439011} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ca0f560-582b-5ed2-ae44-d30f3b653470" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437966} {:answer/id #uuid "0a6fcbcf-baa0-52ca-98cd-0ff0fd8d97f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a6fcbcf-baa0-52ca-98cd-0ff0fd8d97f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437967} :answer-field/id #uuid "26f1c7da-9254-5126-a28b-3e9af246aaa4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439012}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9c8904e1-5f17-5951-8dbc-61b76cd0babc" :question/math-academy-id "q-141088" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{4x}{{e}^{y/2}}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{4x}$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{x} \\\\  & \\ne \\frac{1}{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ and ${y}^{′}=\\frac{4}{x}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4x}{{e}^{y/2}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4x}{{e}^{(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)/2}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4x}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4x}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4x}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{x} & =\\frac{4}{x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272202 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3562e5cf-f895-5f46-86d8-1f4d377e852c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437968} {:answer/id #uuid "54204ebf-cf84-5ca0-9a31-05ad473701a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3562e5cf-f895-5f46-86d8-1f4d377e852c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437968} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b4d80e4-40c9-5772-9f3f-8334efd87237" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439013} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47f8cc69-64ad-5f3d-990f-9498a8c363e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437970} {:answer/id #uuid "2c072334-a0f1-5100-a69e-a1a0ab21bc24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c072334-a0f1-5100-a69e-a1a0ab21bc24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437971} :answer-field/id #uuid "275a3437-057b-583e-8933-7c02f90a39d2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439014} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ca6983f-28cb-5d2b-9d76-a0663297c3a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437972} {:answer/id #uuid "a63eedbc-25e0-50eb-944b-f8fe7cfea503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a63eedbc-25e0-50eb-944b-f8fe7cfea503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437973} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce33855e-6605-5dff-989b-b31182ec13fc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439015}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8806c061-892c-5fd2-baf1-cd903aa5ea31" :question/math-academy-id "q-141089" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{2y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=-3{x}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=-5x$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=-3{x}^{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(-3{x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =-6x \\\\  & \\ne -5x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=-3{x}^{2}$ and ${y}^{′}=-6x$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2y}{x} \\\\ -6x & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2(-3{x}^{2})}{x} \\\\ -6x & =-6x\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=-3{x}^{2}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494077 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0077f4e-bfef-5c44-9c4f-22e790c66054" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494118} {:answer/id #uuid "f470c94f-5751-5b47-a030-8985df3f2d47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f470c94f-5751-5b47-a030-8985df3f2d47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494120} :answer-field/id #uuid "276d5850-899a-5418-b118-58774ff396c5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494089} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0427735-f1b6-5953-9a58-65ffe3fc0cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494104} {:answer/id #uuid "d93ba829-e163-58c2-b76e-e291c5f8be1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494113}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d93ba829-e163-58c2-b76e-e291c5f8be1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494113} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bc47d48-c82a-5502-bb58-b7f089ff6b6b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494102} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c3effa8-82fb-5fb4-8d49-078df0fff8cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494098} {:answer/id #uuid "fbb4386c-3ca1-56b1-a1f1-27eda3db5ebb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbb4386c-3ca1-56b1-a1f1-27eda3db5ebb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494122} :answer-field/id #uuid "b26b8e2c-d5f7-5d56-ac89-1e186c2dea2a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494107}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "03ad73f2-dfe8-5b7e-bde4-05067dff734f" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{3y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=-2{x}^{3}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=-5{x}^{2}$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=-2{x}^{3},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(-2{x}^{3})}^{′} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =-6{x}^{2} \\\\  & \\ne -5{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=-2{x}^{3}$ and ${y}^{′}=-6{x}^{2}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3y}{x} \\\\ -6{x}^{2} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3(-2{x}^{3})}{x} \\\\ -6{x}^{2} & =-6{x}^{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=-2{x}^{3}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494079 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4330cfb7-8007-5f4b-b65a-6b8ca9b8b25b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494094} {:answer/id #uuid "8a470ecb-d8a1-5134-bd03-7aa6af28cd48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a470ecb-d8a1-5134-bd03-7aa6af28cd48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494101} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fa5a541-2f14-5a90-830a-7537bc62c9fb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494083} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b03c25e-572f-53bd-97e2-15a9854478d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494078} {:answer/id #uuid "0f7c5231-f859-571c-a776-7421b5e237a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f7c5231-f859-571c-a776-7421b5e237a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494082} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb07b3e8-17e8-5b30-abe1-b3a39619c2f2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494121} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03474253-5656-59c7-960b-e9aba91c42ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494076} {:answer/id #uuid "11106314-0b0c-5cc0-8770-31f953a783d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11106314-0b0c-5cc0-8770-31f953a783d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494084} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff565a42-5b9c-5eb8-9aec-af09e3750902" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494123}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0e664db5-8912-5df5-8f6f-f040a4a2e7d5" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{4y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=-3{x}^{4}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=-7{x}^{3}$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=-3{x}^{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(-3{x}^{4})}^{′} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 4{x}^{3} \\\\  & =-12{x}^{3} \\\\  & \\ne -7{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=-3{x}^{4}$ and ${y}^{′}=-12{x}^{3}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4y}{x} \\\\ -12{x}^{3} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4(-3{x}^{4})}{x} \\\\ -12{x}^{3} & =-12{x}^{3}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=-3{x}^{4}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494086 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "192c604d-bfad-57a9-aafa-28af0b84c8fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494085} {:answer/id #uuid "e3015e48-583f-5d26-b429-b782d116b88a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "192c604d-bfad-57a9-aafa-28af0b84c8fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494085} :answer-field/id #uuid "22e46930-92a0-561f-be02-0e67f2899630" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494087} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6fff5d8-3756-555b-87b0-8b2c81ddc8ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494106} {:answer/id #uuid "d7d998fe-c81d-521a-aa9f-1f3774a325b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6fff5d8-3756-555b-87b0-8b2c81ddc8ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494106} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b950f16-b0aa-5f58-8c29-f018050c8128" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494090} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40eb77e9-b368-50ce-9757-312b75ebf09b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494093} {:answer/id #uuid "69de21a5-a160-563e-a1e5-f856ad752b34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494100}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40eb77e9-b368-50ce-9757-312b75ebf09b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494093} :answer-field/id #uuid "d961e701-76e1-559b-8cba-a78f269ed6ef" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494114}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "22250596-3a65-57bc-811f-38c308a05ad0" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{2y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=-4{x}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=-6x$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=-4{x}^{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(-4{x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =-8x \\\\  & \\ne -6x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=-4{x}^{2}$ and ${y}^{′}=-8x$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2y}{x} \\\\ -8x & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2(-4{x}^{2})}{x} \\\\ -8x & =-8x\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=-4{x}^{2}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494088 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ed271bf-d92d-5f0f-8661-cf90a21fd2c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/va