259e28d6-9a87-555f-961a-c712d1726ac4" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{2y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=-5{x}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=-7x$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=-5{x}^{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(-5{x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =-5\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =-10x \\\\  & \\ne -7x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=-5{x}^{2}$ and ${y}^{′}=-10x$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2y}{x} \\\\ -10x & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2(-5{x}^{2})}{x} \\\\ -10x & =-10x\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=-5{x}^{2}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494099 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "011418b9-1534-59df-abe2-f6a8f8a26db8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494074} {:answer/id #uuid "021de50f-ea33-579e-a44c-452e1f743ed0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "021de50f-ea33-579e-a44c-452e1f743ed0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494075} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4d4fa50-0